      "content": "The exhaustion you feel is completely valid, and the idea of rebuilding when everything feels deleted is almost impossibly huge. It's a very natural conclusion to feel that fighting is pointless when the landscape has changed so fundamentally. If the world feels shut to you, perhaps the smallest, most immediate act of self-care—something that doesn't require \"building\" anything—could be a starting point. Even a tiny gesture toward yourself can be a quiet act of defiance against the silence.",
